---
import { isPublicPublication } from '../lib/publication/scope';
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import release from '../../config/release.json';
import { assetUrl } from '../lib/evidence';
---
<SiteLayout title="Rights & attribution" description="Reserved rights, material-specific notices and dependency licences for Ardor Lite's reviewed derivatives and independently authored synthetic examples." type="publication">
<header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Publication / Rights</span><h1>Attribution travels<br />with the evidence.</h1><p class="lede">Ardor's source research declares Proprietary. The reviewed package provides selected authored derivatives and independent synthetic demonstrations. Explanations and {isPublicPublication ? 'selected source metadata' : 'selected source excerpts'} are separate from historical research results. Reserved rights remain in force.</p></header>
<div class="prose"><h2>Reviewed derivatives</h2><p>Narratives and figure inputs are sanitized derivatives, not complete originals. Original sources are identified by repository-relative provenance labels and actual SHA-256 hashes. A derivative's inclusion does not grant rights to complete reports, vendor data, price rows, source engines, TradeX ports or Pine scripts.</p><p>Included newly authored summaries and independent examples retain reserved rights. No blanket open-source licence is inferred or granted for Ardor, this website's code or the reviewed package.</p><p><a href={assetUrl('NOTICE.md')}>Read the reviewed package notice</a>.</p><h2>Selected source excerpts</h2><p>{isPublicPublication ? 'The public edition omits five selected Momentum excerpts and 23 selected engineering/Bridge excerpts because their permissions remain local-only.' : 'The publication embeds five selected Momentum excerpts and 23 selected engineering/Bridge excerpts to explain selected implementation details.'} {isPublicPublication ? 'Source identities, line locators and recorded full-file/excerpt hashes are available. Captured text and the local-only Trend supplement inputs/dates are absent and are not reverified by this build. Independent synthetic adaptations remain available.' : 'Captured text, line ranges, full-file hashes and excerpt hashes identify these current-source materials.'} They remain outside the immutable snapshot and the reviewed download map. Capture identity does not prove historical execution identity or permission for public redistribution.</p><p>Permission to cite a source label does not grant permission to redistribute its contents. Excerpts retain their material-specific restrictions. Public embedding clearance for these excerpts remains unresolved. No complete source engine or new source download is offered.</p><h2>Independent method examples</h2><p>Five Python demonstrations were authored independently from public mathematics and reviewed method contracts. They are not untouched historical source implementations. Each method page retains its conceptual-source identities, changes, limitations and reproduction boundary.</p><p><a href={assetUrl('methods/ATTRIBUTION.json')}>Method attribution</a> · <a href={assetUrl('NOTICE.md')}>Method notice</a></p><h2>Fonts and icons</h2><p>Inter, Source Serif 4 and JetBrains Mono are hosted locally. Lucide supplies the small local icon subset. These materials retain their own licences:</p><ul><li><a href="/notices/inter-LICENSE.txt">Inter font licence</a></li><li><a href="/notices/source-serif-4-LICENSE.txt">Source Serif 4 font licence</a></li><li><a href="/notices/jetbrains-mono-LICENSE.txt">JetBrains Mono font licence</a></li><li><a href="/notices/lucide-LICENSE.txt">Lucide ISC licence</a></li></ul><h2>Dependencies</h2><p>The publication is built with Astro, TypeScript and Pagefind; four optional recorded-value views use Observable Plot. All reading assets are served locally, with no live market service or remotely hosted font.</p><p><a href="/notices/dependencies.json">Dependency notice inventory</a></p><h2>Project ownership</h2><p><strong>{release.author.name}</strong> · {release.author.role}.</p><p>{release.author.contributions}</p>{release.author.attribution && Object.entries(release.author.attribution).map(([,credit]) => <p>{credit}</p>)}{isPublicPublication && <p>Independent scientific, reader and device reviews remain incomplete. This publication does not establish research certification, reader effectiveness or a certified or live strategy.</p>}</div>
</SiteLayout>
